# ISO 5457:1999 – Sizes and Layout of Drawing Sheets

general:
  standard: ISO 5457:1999
  title: Technical Product Documentation — Sizes and Layout of Drawing Sheets
  scope: Specifies size and layout of preprinted sheets for technical drawings, including CAD-generated documents
  replaced: ISO 5457:1980
  related_standards:
    - ISO 128-20: Line conventions
    - ISO 216: Paper sizes (A-series)
    - ISO 3098-1: Lettering
    - ISO 7200: Title blocks

sheet_formats:
  series: ISO-A
  preferred_use: Smallest sheet allowing clarity and resolution
  orientation:
    A0–A3: Horizontal (landscape)
    A4: Vertical (portrait)
  reading_direction: Same as title block (bottom-right corner)

borders:
  left_margin: 20 mm (includes filing margin)
  other_margins: 10 mm (top, right, bottom)
  tolerance: ±0.5 mm for trimmed sheets (per ISO 216)

drawing_space_frame:
  line_type: Continuous thick line
  line_width: 0.7 mm
  position: Inner edge of borders
  corner_style: Right-angled (standard), rounded (optional)

centering_marks:
  quantity: 4 (one at each end of symmetry axes)
  placement: Ends of horizontal and vertical center lines
  line_width: 0.7 mm
  extension: 10 mm beyond drawing frame
  tolerance: ±1 mm symmetry
  note: Additional marks required for sizes larger than A0

trimming_marks:
  purpose: Facilitate manual or automatic trimming
  shape: Two overlapping rectangles (10 mm × 5 mm)
  location: All four corners, within borders
  line_width: 0.7 mm

grid_reference_system:
  purpose: Enable precise location of details, revisions, and views
  layout:
    - Vertical division: Capital letters (top to bottom)
    - Horizontal division: Numbers (left to right)
    - I and O excluded (avoid confusion with 1 and 0)
  field_size: 50 mm (preferred), starting from centering marks
  line_width: 0.35 mm (continuous line)
  position: In border area, outside drawing frame
  offset: 5 mm from drawing frame
  character_size: 3.5 mm
  character_orientation: Vertical (on both sides of sheet)
  field_count:
    A0: 24 (letters) × 16 (numbers)
    A1: 16 × 12
    A2: 12 × 8
    A3: 8 × 6
    A4: 6 × 4
  special_case_A4: Grid references only on top and right side

title_block_location:
  A0–A3: Bottom-right corner of drawing space
  A4: Lower part of drawing space (vertical format)

elongated_formats:
  recommendation: Avoid if possible
  construction: Combine short side of one A-size with long side of a larger A-size
  example: A3×A1 (non-standard elongated sheet)

designation_example:
  description: Preprinted A1 drawing sheet on tracing paper (112.5 g/m²), reverse printed, with title block
  format: "ISO 5457 – A1 – Tracing paper – 112.5 g/m² – Reverse printed – With title block"
